    {
      "id": 101106,
      "name": "DrScott",
      "username": "DrScott",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-05-04T15:00:41.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, Hairtrigger reflexes would allow you to hit the underboss, then the crooked cop comes into play, and then Hairtrigger Reflexes would allow you to hit the Crooked Cop. &nbsp; So your hit on the underboss would do full damage in this case. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Just to clarify, the Crooked Cop is already on the table when the new Underboss is played, so it's not a question of hitting the cop, but whether the cop will protect the underboss. And it looks like not since Expat is hitting the boss during the act of being played.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:29:36.568Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
